1
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:56,097
It's been a while.

2
00:00:57,223 --> 00:00:58,266
You've been well, right?

3
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:02,062
All right, let's get going.

4
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,914
This taxi has
two rules.

5
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:24,292
I occasionally pick up new passengers,

6
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:26,753
but I mostly drive regulars
who book in advance.

7
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:29,547
On the way to their destination,

8
00:01:29,631 --> 00:01:32,258
we listen together
to whatever music they want.

9
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:33,176
'A Song Just for You'

10
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:56,116
You wonder if I make enough for gas
only driving regulars?

11
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:01,121
More people seek out this taxi
than you'd think.

12
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:06,126
There's Gyehyang, who can't sleep
because of insomnia.

13
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:13,716
Changshik, who only wears
clothes others have thrown away.

14
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:17,762
And even Ma Dae-il,
the long-haired barista.

15
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:21,432
Oh, and in the drama,

16
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:24,561
the actress Oh Young-ran,
who plays Matsogeum,

17
00:02:24,644 --> 00:02:26,771
is a regular in this taxi, too.

18
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:30,400
As we drive along,

19
00:02:30,483 --> 00:02:32,694
I take song requests from my passengers.

20
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:36,406
Sometimes their stories
become the lyrics.

21
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:38,116
Sir!

22
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:39,576
Sir!

23
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:43,830
Huh?

24
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:44,998
Every time they get in the back seat,

25
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:47,000
some passengers make a full confession.

26
00:02:52,797 --> 00:02:54,841
Come to think of it, sometimes it's easier

27
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:56,551
to open up to someone
you're not too close to

28
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:59,387
and tell them what's really on your mind.

29
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:00,388
In that sense,

30
00:03:00,471 --> 00:03:03,892
the driver's seat and
the passenger's back seat

31
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:06,144
make for just the right distance.

32
00:03:14,986 --> 00:03:16,946
What do I do when I don't have a booking?

33
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:19,324
Well...

34
00:03:22,452 --> 00:03:24,120
I kill time somewhere

35
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:25,246
while I wait for a booking.

36
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:32,253
I wait for bookings while I eat.

37
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:35,340
Oh, this one, this one, this one.

38
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:36,633
Look, look, look!

39
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:39,302
I wait for bookings
while coaching the players.

40
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:45,892
I wait for bookings,
savoring the aroma of coffee.

41
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:44,701
Yeon-woo?

42
00:05:03,928 --> 00:05:06,764
This is Yeon-woo,
one of my regulars.

43
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:10,393
Whenever she goes through a breakup,

44
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:11,936
she books a taxi.

45
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:15,106
Every time I pick her up,

46
00:05:15,189 --> 00:05:16,858
my heart feels heavy.

47
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:21,446
Driver...

48
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,741
Just take me anywhere.

49
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:27,201
Today...

50
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:29,495
Did she break up again?

51
00:05:58,941 --> 00:06:00,693
You changed your hair.

52
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:03,112
Short hair suits you, too.

53
00:06:07,658 --> 00:06:08,826
Thank you.

54
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:13,664
I was wondering...

55
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:16,250
Did you cut your hair
because of a breakup...?

56
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:19,253
He's the absolute worst.

57
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:23,424
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have said
something so... so insensitive.

58
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:26,594
No, I mean...

59
00:06:28,304 --> 00:06:30,640
That jerk is the absolute worst.

60
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:03,047
Hurry up, babe!

61
00:07:12,515 --> 00:07:14,976
What? You bought four?

62
00:07:15,643 --> 00:07:17,854
I didn't know which flavor you'd like.

63
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:20,314
These are cinnamon—one with
sugar, one without.

64
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:21,941
- These are chocolate, one with sugar.
- Oh, my!

65
00:07:22,024 --> 00:07:22,859
And one without.

66
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:24,777
Pick whichever one you want most.

67
00:07:24,861 --> 00:07:26,446
I'll eat the rest.

68
00:07:27,071 --> 00:07:28,531
Oh, stop it.

69
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:29,866
I'm gonna cry.

70
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:31,534
Oh, what are you saying?

71
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:34,162
Come on.

72
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:39,167
Hey, Teddy,
could you carry these two for me?

73
00:07:41,752 --> 00:07:42,587
Thanks.

74
00:07:44,338 --> 00:07:45,631
Teddy?

75
00:07:49,385 --> 00:07:50,970
Okay, I'll take it.

76
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:55,558
Oh...

77
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:57,185
Like an idiot...

78
00:07:57,768 --> 00:08:01,481
Getting stuck taking a commemorative
photo between those two...

79
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:06,402
Ugh, this is so annoying.

80
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:10,239
Ugh, this is so annoying.

81
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:15,453
It's only been three days
since he broke up with me.

82
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:19,457
Could you take one vertically, too?

83
00:08:21,876 --> 00:08:23,211
One, two...

84
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:25,254
- Huh? Uh, uh...
- Oh, huh?

85
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:27,340
Huh.

86
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:39,268
Oh, what was that?

87
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:40,478
I don't know.

88
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:55,201
We've arrived.

89
00:08:58,663 --> 00:08:59,872
Where are we?

90
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:01,874
The zoo.

91
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:07,380
This place suits me.

92
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:13,636
Driver.

93
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:17,056
Could you wait here for a little while?

94
00:10:48,022 --> 00:10:49,398
Oh, goodness. Oh, goodness.

95
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:51,192
- Oh, dear, oh, dear.
- Oh...

96
00:10:51,275 --> 00:10:53,027
- It's okay.
- Someone might think...

97
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:55,738
we're kidnapping a bear from the zoo.

98
00:10:56,405 --> 00:10:58,449
Actually, I was walking
around in this earlier...

99
00:10:58,532 --> 00:11:01,077
I hurriedly took it off in case someone
shot me with a tranquilizer dart.

100
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:04,163
Oh, that was really dangerous.

101
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:05,247
- Exactly.

102
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:08,668
There, all cleaned up?

103
00:11:08,751 --> 00:11:09,669
Oh.

104
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:12,380
There's a pocket for personal
items inside this mascot suit.

105
00:11:12,463 --> 00:11:14,340
You know, my phone, makeup...

106
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:18,594
I've got lots of candy in there, too,
for when my blood sugar dips at work.

107
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:19,804
Oh...

108
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:31,982
He said he liked short hair.

109
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,484
So I cut mine.

110
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:36,987
But the woman I saw him with
today had long, straight hair.

111
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:45,704
He said women with long, straight hair looked
like ghosts, so he wouldn't even look at them.

112
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:51,877
And he'd only give me
perfume in scents he liked.

113
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:58,968
I hate musk.

114
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:01,971
- Yeon-woo.
- Yeah?

115
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:04,223
I'm the one who has to smell
it, after all.

116
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:07,059
So I realized I should
pick a scent I like.

117
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:09,770
Yeah.

118
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:12,106
I'm always trying to
accommodate the other person.

119
00:12:12,189 --> 00:12:13,691
I really try hard, you know?

120
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:17,361
But today, it suddenly hit me.

121
00:12:18,195 --> 00:12:19,029
'Oh...'

122
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:24,577
'Maybe I only cared about being who
the other person wanted me to be.'

123
00:12:26,245 --> 00:12:27,955
Maybe that man

124
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:32,168
has never seen the real you, Yeon-woo.

125
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:36,964
What I like...

126
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:39,258
and what I don't like.

127
00:12:41,051 --> 00:12:44,346
I've never tried to show
him who I really am,

128
00:12:45,347 --> 00:12:47,224
just as I am.

129
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:50,936
I was afraid he'd hate the real me.

130
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:58,110
Even when I was dating, I was always

131
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,447
hiding deep inside that bear costume.

132
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:12,917
Driver.

133
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,211
I'd like to hear this song today.

134
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:19,423
Oh, The Black Skirts are great!

135
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:20,966
You know The Black Skirts?

136
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:24,720
I have a pretty broad musical range.

137
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:27,681
I always buy The Black Skirts' albums.

138
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:29,850
Though they don't put
out albums very often.

139
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:33,270
No, I always kept you in mind, Driver,

140
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:36,357
and asked for songs I thought you'd know.

141
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:39,360
Yes, I noticed you always did that.

142
00:13:39,443 --> 00:13:40,903
It honestly made me feel a little hurt.

143
00:13:48,869 --> 00:13:49,703
Here.

144
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:51,539
Ta-da!

145
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:03,217
♪ By tomorrow ♪

146
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:07,680
♪ The people who'll leave me ♪

147
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:11,934
♪ Aren't who I'm worried ♪

148
00:14:13,727 --> 00:14:16,564
♪ About ♪

149
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:20,860
♪ By tomorrow ♪

150
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:25,281
♪ I'll be across the sea again ♪

151
00:14:26,824 --> 00:14:29,869
♪ Left all alone ♪

152
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:33,956
♪ Will you be all right? ♪

153
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:38,294
♪ Into my ear ♪

154
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:42,590
♪ Sing a song for me ♪

155
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:47,136
♪ So I won't hear ♪

156
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:51,557
♪ The other birds sing ♪

157
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:56,020
♪ My one and only ♪

158
00:14:57,187 --> 00:15:00,608
♪ Love, as I leave it behind ♪

159
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:04,737
♪ The handkerchief ♪

160
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:09,575
♪ You'd kept hidden, wave goodbye ♪

161
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:12,703
♪ Oh ♪

162
00:15:12,786 --> 00:15:18,250
♪ Hey, let your bright light
shine on me ♪

163
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:22,671
♪ Can you love me
unconditionally? ♪

164
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:29,053
♪ And sing a million lullabies
on a sleepy day ♪

165
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:35,726
♪ Hey, let your sea breeze
blow on me ♪

166
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:40,230
♪ When I am sailing
internationally ♪

167
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:41,148
♪ And whisper... ♪

168
00:15:41,231 --> 00:15:44,276
Oh? Driver,
not right in front of my house.

169
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:46,904
Could you drop me off
up there instead?

170
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:48,530
- Right there, here.
- Uh...

171
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:49,448
Yes.

172
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:54,787
Huh?

173
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:56,413
I said I'd get out here?

174
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:58,457
Well, earlier at the zoo,

175
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,334
I left the meter running,
and the fare really piled up.

176
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:04,254
Oh! I'll cover the dryer, too.

177
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:05,172
Oh...

178
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:09,051
D-Driver, the fare must've
been pretty high today, right?

179
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:10,302
Yes.

180
00:16:10,386 --> 00:16:13,013
You could probably take tomorrow off
and not accept any bookings.

181
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:20,145
Oh, dear.

182
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:34,702
What should I say?

183
00:16:36,203 --> 00:16:37,496
Just...

184
00:16:37,579 --> 00:16:39,415
Tell them exactly what happened.

185
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:47,715
Oh, okay.

186
00:16:48,465 --> 00:16:50,175
I'm sorry.

187
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:52,094
Yes, yes. I'm sorry.

188
00:16:52,761 --> 00:16:53,595
Yes.

189
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:56,890
Oh...

190
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:06,734
First,

191
00:17:07,484 --> 00:17:09,486
they said to return that teddy bear first.

192
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:12,322
What, do they think I'll run
off without returning it?

193
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:14,825
If I get fired,
I'll just find another part-time job.

194
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:17,494
I don't want to...

195
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:20,122
wear a mascot costume anymore.

196
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:21,999
Yes.

197
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:25,878
Thank you.

198
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:26,795
All right.

199
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:27,880
Cheers!

200
00:17:47,357 --> 00:17:49,234
Okay, let's take the palace.

201
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:50,694
Aw, come on.

202
00:17:52,196 --> 00:17:53,655
Oh! Uh, uh, uh, uh!

203
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:56,158
K-K-Knight... oh...

204
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:00,079
Whoa!

205
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:01,789
Checkmate!

206
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:04,500
- Check! Check! Take that!
- Damn it.

207
00:18:05,501 --> 00:18:06,376
Aw...

208
00:18:07,377 --> 00:18:08,670
All right. Ha ha.

209
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:10,380
Oh, damn.

210
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:12,174
A regular of mine, and

211
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:14,593
a collector of breakups,
Yeon-woo, is calling.

212
00:18:15,719 --> 00:18:18,972
What kind of breakup
has she had this time?

213
00:18:24,978 --> 00:18:26,730
I've heard a lot about you.

214
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:29,316
Yeon-woo said you've helped her a lot whenever
she's been going through a hard time.

215
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:31,193
Oh.

216
00:18:31,276 --> 00:18:32,569
Oh, it was nothing.

217
00:18:32,653 --> 00:18:35,823
I just make sure she gets home
safely, that's all.

218
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:37,741
For some reason,

219
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:40,494
I wanted you to meet my boyfriend, sir.

220
00:18:42,037 --> 00:18:44,414
You know my whole story
better than anyone.

221
00:18:45,666 --> 00:18:46,500
Well...

222
00:18:47,376 --> 00:18:49,711
What do you think?
Doesn't this one seem like it'll last?

223
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:52,589
If things always went the way I said,

224
00:18:52,673 --> 00:18:54,591
I'd be a fortune-teller,
not a taxi driver.

225
00:18:54,675 --> 00:18:57,344
Come on, you must have a gut feeling.

226
00:18:58,637 --> 00:19:00,139
My gut says it's looking good.

227
00:19:00,222 --> 00:19:03,100
And you're even going on a
weekend date at an amusement park.

228
00:19:03,183 --> 00:19:04,726
Mm-hmm.

229
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:06,019
We're heading to work.

230
00:19:07,229 --> 00:19:08,397
We're coworkers dating.

231
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:10,482
Oh?

232
00:19:11,066 --> 00:19:13,819
Oh, so you're still
wearing the mascot costume?

233
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:16,572
No, I ditched the mascot costume.

234
00:19:17,447 --> 00:19:18,448
That day,

235
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:21,410
I took your advice and was
honest about everything,

236
00:19:21,493 --> 00:19:23,787
and told my manager the whole truth.

237
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:26,123
So my manager switched
me to a different role.

238
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:27,207
Thanks to that,

239
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:29,209
I got to meet my honey here, too.

240
00:19:29,793 --> 00:19:30,711
Hee-hee!

241
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:32,296
Oh!

242
00:19:36,258 --> 00:19:37,885
All right, everyone...

243
00:19:37,968 --> 00:19:41,263
What's the part everyone's been
waiting for at Black Hole 2000?

244
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:42,973
Dance time!

245
00:19:43,056 --> 00:19:45,559
We're going to get started now.

246
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:47,060
Let's go!

247
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:50,522
♪ Hol, hol, Black Hole
Fly away, Black Hole ♪

248
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:53,400
♪ Spinning round as you go in,
coming out with a big grin ♪

249
00:19:53,483 --> 00:19:56,570
♪ Hol, hol, Black Hole
Fly away, Black Hole ♪

250
00:19:56,653 --> 00:19:57,905
♪ The two of you side by side ♪

251
00:19:57,988 --> 00:19:59,323
♪ Heart-pounding Black Hole ♪

252
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:02,451
♪ Hol, hol, Black Hole
Fly away, Black Hole ♪

253
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:04,953
♪ Fall in love, Black Hole
Forever love, Black Hole ♪

254
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:08,248
♪ Hol, hol, Black Hole ♪

255
00:20:08,332 --> 00:20:10,709
♪ Holololol, Black Hole ♪

256
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:12,961
Let's go!

257
00:20:14,421 --> 00:20:15,464
Ho, ho!

258
00:20:17,966 --> 00:20:19,968
Uh, aren't we setting off?

259
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:24,723
All right.

260
00:20:24,806 --> 00:20:28,393
Let's keep this energy going
and set off.

261
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:29,978
Let's go!

262
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:35,442
Bye!

263
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,945
Ho!

264
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:38,987
Wow.

265
00:20:39,071 --> 00:20:41,949
♪ By tomorrow ♪

266
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:46,286
♪ The ones who'll leave me behind ♪

267
00:20:47,829 --> 00:20:50,540
♪ I'm not worried ♪

268
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:55,128
♪ About them ♪

269
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:59,466
